# S3 — fmt. THE CALIBRATION CANDIDATE (Gate B), not a work candidate.
# Campaign 1, frozen 2026-07-24 (§2, §4).
#
# The truthful answer for this class is already measured: 298 priceable
# functions against 744 sole-blockers (2026-07-20 fmt probe, v1.37.0
# population). Running it through the sweep yields the ceiling/truth ratio that
# every other candidate's number is read against. Above 3x fires the kill
# switch against the instrument itself.
#
# fmt is pinned unverifiable in the real cost table on purpose: formatting cost
# depends on the VALUES, not the format string. O(1) here is deliberately
# false.
fmt.Sprintf O(1)
fmt.Errorf O(1)
